; ✅ RESOLVED 2026-07-16 — VERIFIED ALL WIDTHS + NESTED POSITIONS BY CONTENT on trunk b6aefb20e. v-patterns box-widen fix (24293bec9, Inc-53): is_narrow_int gains strip_nominal → the CENTRAL widen-before-box-int helper now widens an erased narrow newtype (Ty::Nominal(W,Int u8)) before box-int, fixing ALL nested positions at the source. VERIFIED VALID: UInt8/Int8/Int16/Int32 list-element (was INVALID i32-in-if-i64), Int64 control, tuple-nested UInt8 — all compile to valid wasm. This was the CONSTRUCTION-side root (breaker locus guess of the list desugar was wrong; the real fix is the shared boxing helper) — answers breaker systemic 3rd-re-hardcode worry (compare-side per-path a1510c912/6e2aebd13 + this construction-side central = family closed). v-patterns adding tuple+sum graded cases. CLOSED.
